    "result_text": "The build succeeds with all tests green. The three test files are `AcceptanceTest`, `AcceptanceBase` (abstract, not a test), and one supporting file \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only runnable test class, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field so that `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nSince the API response type `OwnerDto` is generated from the OpenAPI spec and populated via a MapStruct mapper (the same pattern used by the existing `displayName` field), I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema, mirroring `displayName`, so the generated `OwnerDto` includes the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `initials` backed by a new `toInitials` method (with a small `initial()` helper) that upper-cases the first character of each name and joins them with dots:\n   ```\n   john + smith \u2192 \"J.\" + \"S.\" \u2192 \"J.S.\"\n   ```\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreComputesInitials` and the full test suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
